From 3f12f6132d43a70e7500d52d1f6331a6f2bb705b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:19:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lightrec code cache; Lightning memory reuse and dcbz clearing

- Blocks retired because their code was overwritten are kept with their
  compiled code (up to 4096 blocks, 2 MiB of code, oldest dropped first) and
  taken back when exactly the same MIPS code (a copy is made with each block)
  returns at the same address: no compile. Dropped first when the code buffer
  is full.
- Lightning's buffers of 1 KiB and more are kept by size when freed and
  handed out again, and cleared a cache line at a time with dcbz (line size
  probed once): each compile allocated and cleared about 75 KB.
  (JIT_MEM_CACHE, on for the PS3)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HyAyv1PvGqyTegufofF5fp
